  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "At present, neither etag or the fedora state token are returned when making requests within a transaction. So a client is unable to tell that the state of resource which is being used for read only purposes in a transaction is unchanged, and therefore cached versions may be used. Accessing the same state of a resource in and outside of a transaction gives different cache headers.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Additionally, no last modified header is returned in a transaction, which makes optimistic locking when inside of a transaction impossible. So it would be helpful to provide up to date last-modified headers.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So from the perspective of a client, it would be helpful to return these headers when making requests within a transaction.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
